FX  - This paper is in memory of Prof. Jianwu Tang (1970 -2023) for his pioneering contributions to blue carbon research. His groundbreaking work expanded our scientific understanding of coastal blue carbon, inspired many researchers to work toward mitigating the impacts of climate change, and his unwavering support for young scientists will be his enduring legacy. He will be greatly missed, and his in fluence will continue to inspire us to explore new frontiers in ecological research. This work is funded by the CAS Project for Young Scientists in Basic Research (YSBR-037) , ANSO collaborative research (ANSO-CR-KP-2022-11) , the National Natural Science Foundation of China (U2106209, 42141003, 42141016, and 32171594) , the Guangdong Basic and Applied Basic Research Foundation (2021B1515020011 and 2021B1212110004) , the CAS Youth Innovation Promotion Association (2021347) , the National Forestry and Grassland Administration Youth Talent Support Program (2020BJ003) , and the R&D program of Guangdong Provincial Department of Science and Technology (2018B030324003) .
